# ============================================================
# NETLIFY REDIRECTS
# ============================================================
# Netlify serves this repo root exactly as it is committed, so
# every file in the repo is fetchable over HTTP unless a rule
# with a bang shadows it. These rules bounce the files that are
# not meant for the public back to the homepage.
#
# The band documents function holds every Drive link in one
# file. Without the block below, anyone could download that
# source at /netlify/functions/roadcase-links.mjs and read the
# lot without signing in. Do not remove it.
#
# On 2026-08-22 this file was replaced wholesale by an upload
# that kept only the two netlify.app host rules. That deleted
# the /netlify/* block and left the function source public for
# about an hour, and it dropped the five old Squarespace URL
# rules so /home 404'd and /about, /tour, /fan-photos and
# /band-gallery answered 200 at two URLs each. Restored here.
# Edit this file in the repo, not through a whole-file upload.
#
# The functions themselves are invoked at
# /.netlify/functions/<name>, with a leading dot, which none of
# these rules touch.
# ============================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# HOST CANONICALISATION
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Netlify already 301s the netlify.app subdomain to the apex
# because apex is set as the primary domain. These rules make
# it explicit and survive a change to that setting. Apex is
# canonical, no www.
# ------------------------------------------------------------

https://britishinvasionyears.netlify.app/*  https://britishinvasionyears.com/:splat  301!
http://britishinvasionyears.netlify.app/*   https://britishinvasionyears.com/:splat  301!

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# OLD SQUARESPACE URLS
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# The old site used extensionless URLs, this one uses .html.
# Netlify's extensionless fallback would already SERVE the right
# page at /about, but it answers 200, not 301. These rules make
# the move explicit so Google retires the old URL and hands the
# ranking to the .html page the canonicals point at.
#
# /home is the only one that genuinely 404s without a rule. The
# old homepage lived there, this one is at /.
#
# THE BANG ON THE FOUR .html RULES IS LOAD BEARING. Netlify only
# consults a redirect rule when nothing already answers the path,
# and its extensionless fallback resolves /about to about.html
# first, so an unforced rule never fires and the URL keeps
# answering 200. Verified live on 2026-08-15, and re-verified on
# 2026-08-22 when their removal put all four back to 200.
#
# THIS LIST IS THE FIVE URLS VERIFIED IN DOMAIN-CUTOVER.md STEP 4.
# It is not proven to be every URL the old site had. Before the
# old site goes dark, pull the real inventory from Squarespace or
# from Search Console coverage and add anything missing here.
# ------------------------------------------------------------

/home                 /                  301
/about                /about.html        301!
/tour                 /tour.html         301!
/fan-photos           /fan-photos.html   301!
/band-gallery         /band-gallery.html 301!

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# BLOG POST URLS
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Posts moved from post.html?slug=<x> to /blog/<x>.html on
# 2026-08-31, when they were switched from client-side render
# to real pre-rendered files. The old form was in sitemap.xml,
# on every tour card's WHAT TO DO IN TOWN button, and in the
# MusicEvent subjectOf, so it has inbound links and index
# entries to hand over.
#
# THE BANG IS LOAD BEARING for the same reason it is on the
# Squarespace rules above: post.html still exists as a file, so
# Netlify answers it before ever consulting a redirect. Without
# the bang the old URL keeps returning 200 and the move never
# reaches Google.
#
# post.html is kept on purpose rather than deleted. It still
# renders any post client-side, so if a rule here is ever
# dropped the content is reachable instead of 404.
# ------------------------------------------------------------

/post.html  slug=:slug  /blog/:slug.html  301!
/post.html              /blog.html        301!

# Build machinery. Not public.
/tools/*              /    301!
/netlify.toml         /    301!

# Function source, including every band document link.
/netlify/*            /    301!

# The Netlify config files themselves.
/_headers             /    301!
/_redirects           /    301!

# Internal runbook. Lists the GA4 property, the Formspree
# endpoint, and the repo. Not for the public.
/DOMAIN-CUTOVER.md    /    301!
